proposed_comments.body:
**[P2] Persist the accepted key independently of runtime equality**

When setup has already changed `Encryption.MyKey`, this guard can skip `settings.MyKey`, leaving the previously stored key to be restored on reload. It also treats a case-only edit as unchanged even though `GenLegalKey` passes the exact key string to PBKDF2. Persist `settings.MyKey` outside the runtime-change guard and compare the runtime value with `StringComparison.Ordinal`.

```suggestion
            if (!newKey.Equals(Encryption.MyKey, StringComparison.Ordinal))
            {
                Encryption.MyKey = newKey;
                Encryption.GeneratedKey = false;
            }

            settings.MyKey = newKey;
```

